.SH "NAME"
man-new \- create or edit a personal man page, authored in AsciiDoc
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.sp
\fBman\-new\fP [\fB\-\-from\-help\fP] \fIname\fP [\fIsection\fP]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.sp
Creates a new man page source under
\f(CR~/.local/share/man\-src/man<section>/<name>.adoc\fP
using a minimal AsciiDoc template, opens it in \fI$EDITOR\fP, then compiles it
with \fBasciidoctor\fP into
\f(CR~/.local/share/man/man<section>/<name>.<section>\fP.
.sp
If the source file already exists, no template is written and the existing
file is opened as\-is, so \fBman\-new\fP also works as a quick "edit and recompile
this page" command.
.sp
Both the AsciiDoc source and the compiled page live under
\f(CR~/.local/share\fP, which is symlinked into the \fBdotfiles\fP git repository, so
edits are version\-controlled and pushed to GitHub along with the rest of the
dotfiles.
.sp
With \fB\-\-from\-help\fP, the initial template is seeded from
\f(CR<name> \-\-help\fP and \f(CR<name> \-\-version\fP instead of a blank page: the usage
block becomes SYNOPSIS, and single\-line "flag, gap, description" option
lines (the GNU\-style format used by tools like \fBstow\fP and \fBjq\fP) are turned
into OPTIONS entries automatically. This is a heuristic, not a full parser \(em tools that print an option\(cqs description on a separate line from its
flag (the clap/cobra style used by tools like \fBripgrep\fP) won\(cqt get
auto\-populated OPTIONS. Either way, the full raw \f(CR\-\-help\fP output is always
appended under a HELP OUTPUT section so nothing is lost; delete it once
you\(cqve folded what you need into DESCRIPTION/OPTIONS by hand.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.sp
\fB\-\-from\-help\fP
.RS 4
Seed the template from \f(CR<name> \-\-help\fP/\f(CR\-\-version\fP instead of a blank
page. Requires \fIname\fP to be an executable on \f(CR$PATH\fP.
.RE
.sp
\fIsection\fP
.RS 4
Man section number, e.g. 1 for user commands, 5 for file formats, 8 for
admin commands. Defaults to 1.
.RE
.SH "EXAMPLES"
.sp
\fBman\-new deploy\-check\fP
.RS 4
Creates and opens \f(CR~/.local/share/man\-src/man1/deploy\-check.adoc\fP, then
compiles it to \f(CR~/.local/share/man/man1/deploy\-check.1\fP.
.RE
.sp
\fBman\-new fstab 5\fP
.RS 4
Creates and opens \f(CR~/.local/share/man\-src/man5/fstab.adoc\fP, then compiles
it to \f(CR~/.local/share/man/man5/fstab.5\fP.
.RE
.sp
\fBman\-new \-\-from\-help jq\fP
.RS 4
Seeds \f(CR~/.local/share/man\-src/man1/jq.adoc\fP from \f(CRjq \-\-help\fP/\f(CR\-\-version\fP
before opening it for editing.
.RE
.SH "FILES"
.sp
\f(CR~/.local/bin/man\-new\fP
.RS 4
The script itself.
.RE
.sp
\f(CR~/.local/share/man\-src/man<section>/<name>.adoc\fP
.RS 4
AsciiDoc source.
.RE
.sp
\f(CR~/.local/share/man/man<section>/<name>.<section>\fP
.RS 4
Compiled man page.
.RE
